prompt:
Review pull request 87 in this Node.js scheduling API. The change moves internal clients from session cookies to bearer tokens and touches the route wiring, token handling, tests, and authentication documentation. Read the author's description and exact diff under pr/87, then inspect the surrounding project code and contracts. I need a review before the mobile rollout because errors here would affect every schedule and administration request. Call out concrete defects that matter in this project, explain their consequence, and give a fix a developer can apply. Do not spend the review on broad praise. Write the review to REVIEW.md at the top of the project, and end it with a fenced json list of findings, each with location (path/to/file.ext:LINE, with line numbers of the file as it is in the project), severity (critical, high, medium, low or nit), issue and fix.

```json
[
  { "location": "path/to/file.ext:LINE", "severity": "high", "issue": "what is wrong and why it matters", "fix": "an actionable change" }
]
```
